<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent Blend loading port closed by wind.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent Blend loading port closed by wind.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sullom Voe Brent Blend loading terminal in the North Sea was closed early on Monday because of heavy winds, port officials at Shetland Islands Marine Operations said.</p>
<p>Winds up to 45-50 knots were expected later on Monday, the official said. One vessel was due to sail later in the morning and no tankers were waiting to berth. One crude oil vessel was expected to arrive later in the day.</p>
<p>The terminal handles crude produced from 13 fields and several satellite wells piped to Sullom Voe for blending with Ninian crude and exported as Brent Blend.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7630</p>
